The invention relates to a method (METH) for measuring a distance R between a vehicle (V) and an identifier (I) used for accessing and starting the vehicle (V), wherein the vehicle (V) and the identifier (I) are synchronised. The method (METH) comprises the following steps:

— selecting (Sel_fp) N frequencies fp, pϵ[1;N], where N is a natural number greater than 3;

— performing N sequences Sqp, each sequence Sqp comprising the following steps:

• transmitting (Em_Svp) a first signal (Svp) of frequency fp from an emitter (TXv) of the vehicle (V) to a receiver (Rxi) of the identifier (I);

• measuring (Mes_φvip), by means of a calculator (Xi) of the identifier (I), a phase φvip, modulo 2π, of the received first signal (Svp) relative to a second signal (Sip) having a phase φip(t)=φ0ip+2πfpt;

• transmitting (Em_Sip) the second signal (Sip) from an emitter (TXi) of the identifier (I) to a receiver (RXv) of the vehicle (V);

• calculating (Mes_φivp), by means of a calculator (Xv) of the vehicle (V), a phase φivp, modulo 2π, of the received second signal (Sip) relative to the first signal (Svp);

• calculating (Cal_φp) the average φp of the phase φvip and the phase φivp;

— for each p between 1 and N−1, calculating (Cal_Pp) a ramp Pp according to the formula Pp=(φp+1−φp)/(fp+1−fp); and

— calculating (Cal_R) the distance R from the ramps Pp, pϵ[1;N].

