— choosing (Sel_fp) a set of N frequencies fp, with pϵ[1;N], where N represents a natural number greater than 3;

— carrying out N sequences Sqp, with each individual sequence Sqp involving these operations:

• sending (Em_Svp) an initial signal (Svp) at frequency fp from a transmitter (TXv) located on the vehicle (V) toward a receiver (Rxi) belonging to the identifier (I);

• using a calculator (Xi) within the identifier (I) to measure (Mes_φvip) the phase φvip, modulo 2π, of the received initial signal (Svp), in comparison with a secondary signal (Sip) whose phase is given by φip(t)=φ0ip+2πfpt; sending (Em_Sip) this secondary signal (Sip) from a transmitter (TXi) on the identifier (I) toward a receiver (RXv) on the vehicle (V);

• using a calculator (Xv) within the vehicle (V) to compute (Mes_φivp) the phase φivp, modulo 2π, of the received secondary signal (Sip), relative to the initial signal (Svp);

• determining (Cal_φp) the mean value φp derived from phase φvip and phase φivp;

— for every value of p ranging from 1 to N-1, computing (Cal_Pp) a slope Pp according to the equation Pp=(φp+1−φp)/(fp+1−fp); and

— deriving (Cal_R) the distance R from the collection of slopes Pp, pϵ[1;N].

